          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അളവ് — aḷavŭ — \"a measurement; a size\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തയ്യൽക്കാരൻ എന്റെ അളവ് എടുത്തു. tayyalkkāran enṟe aḷavŭ eṭuttu. The tailor took my measurements."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun of അളക്കുക, to measure. A shirt in your size is നിങ്ങളുടെ അളവിലുള്ള ഷർട്ട്."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അളവ് (aḷavŭ) is native Dravidian, the noun of അളക്കുക, to measure (DEDR 295)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
